From the relation,
$\begin{aligned}
& \overline{\mathrm{KE}}= \frac{3}{2} k T \\
& \Rightarrow \quad \frac{(\overline{\mathrm{KE}})_1}{(\overline{\mathrm{KE}})_2}=\frac{T_1}{T_2} \quad \mathrm{(become k is constant)}
\end{aligned}$
Given, $\quad T_1=300 \mathrm{~K}, T_2=350 \mathrm{~K}\therefore \quad \frac{(\mathrm{KE})_1}{(\mathrm{KE})_2}=\frac{300}{350}=\frac{6}{7}$
